WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:02.969
(light music)

00:00:10.149 --> 00:00:12.779
- [Narrator] Scattered
across the New Mexico desert

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:16.946
are buildings that look like
something from another world.

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:23.349
They are homes

00:00:23.349 --> 00:00:26.109
designed to be completely self-sustained.

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:30.276
Generating their own electricity,
water, gas, and food.

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:36.040
They are the life's work of
an unconventional architect,

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:39.547
Mike Reynolds, who
believes homes are the key

00:00:39.547 --> 00:00:41.130
to a better future.

00:00:46.248 --> 00:00:47.739
- We came up with the name Earthship

00:00:47.739 --> 00:00:51.368
because houses have to
have gas lines coming in,

00:00:51.368 --> 00:00:54.109
sewage lines going out,
electric lines coming in,

00:00:54.109 --> 00:00:57.469
and so these buildings provide
all of that themselves.

00:00:57.469 --> 00:01:00.298
These buildings address
comfortable shelter,

00:01:00.298 --> 00:01:04.465
electricity, water, sewage
treatment, garbage, and food.

00:01:05.669 --> 00:01:07.240
- Michael Reynolds started all this

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:10.618
after the oil crises in the ‘70s.

00:01:10.618 --> 00:01:13.469
Once the prices went up,
that meant everything

00:01:13.469 --> 00:01:15.074
we had to buy just went up.

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:17.240
So this house is basically trying to

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:20.823
make us less dependent
on all these things.

00:01:22.613 --> 00:01:26.780
- I came to Taos right after
architectural school in 1969.

00:01:27.625 --> 00:01:29.923
This climate is super severe.

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:31.772
It's real hot in the summer

00:01:31.772 --> 00:01:34.732
and it's real cold in the winters.

00:01:34.732 --> 00:01:37.974
So it's a perfect place to test pilot

00:01:37.974 --> 00:01:40.273
these buildings so that you see if they

00:01:40.273 --> 00:01:42.105
can stay warm in severe conditions

00:01:42.105 --> 00:01:44.145
and cool in severe conditions.

00:01:44.145 --> 00:01:45.865
There are mountains of automobile tires

00:01:45.865 --> 00:01:47.177
everywhere all over the world.

00:01:47.177 --> 00:01:50.854
Well, why don't we make a use for tires?

00:01:50.854 --> 00:01:54.105
- [Rowan] The tires give out
the foundation of the house

00:01:54.105 --> 00:01:56.214
and also the structural walls.

00:01:56.214 --> 00:01:58.923
- The tire will not rot,
termites don't eat them,

00:01:58.923 --> 00:02:01.612
they are resilient for earthquakes.

00:02:01.612 --> 00:02:03.854
- And at the same time
because they're packed

00:02:03.854 --> 00:02:06.593
with earth inside, it's
going to accumulate the heat.

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:09.145
It's like a heat battery.

00:02:09.145 --> 00:02:12.825
- It sucks up heat and then
it gives it back to you

00:02:12.825 --> 00:02:15.563
when the temperature of the room drops.

00:02:15.563 --> 00:02:18.065
- You do feel really nurtured inside

00:02:18.065 --> 00:02:20.363
some of these houses because
inside the living space,

00:02:20.363 --> 00:02:24.665
the temperature is the
same all year round.

00:02:24.665 --> 00:02:26.803
Then we have plastic and glass bottles.

00:02:26.803 --> 00:02:31.345
We cut them in half and we put
the two bottom ends together.

00:02:31.345 --> 00:02:33.934
It means that we'll be
using much less cement

00:02:33.934 --> 00:02:36.625
because we're using this other
material which compensates.

00:02:36.625 --> 00:02:39.003
At the same time, it's going to let light

00:02:39.003 --> 00:02:40.084
come in to the house.

00:02:40.084 --> 00:02:41.734
You can do combinations of colors,

00:02:41.734 --> 00:02:43.317
you can do mosaics.

00:02:46.534 --> 00:02:47.745
- [Narrator] Reynolds and his team

00:02:47.745 --> 00:02:50.414
have been sharing their
designs around the world,

00:02:50.414 --> 00:02:53.747
developing Earthships in places of need.

00:02:54.793 --> 00:02:57.643
- I lay in bed sometimes awake at night,

00:02:57.643 --> 00:02:59.513
can't wait to get up the next morning

00:02:59.513 --> 00:03:00.772
and keep doing this.

00:03:00.772 --> 00:03:03.492
We're building, we're
drawing, we're traveling,

00:03:03.492 --> 00:03:04.893
doing education.

00:03:04.893 --> 00:03:06.884
I plan to keep going until I drop

00:03:06.884 --> 00:03:08.612
but I'm already seeing,

00:03:08.612 --> 00:03:10.563
that it doesn't matter when I drop,

00:03:10.563 --> 00:03:14.313
there's people that are just gonna
keep doing this.

